# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. All PUBLIC_* vars are read at BUILD
# time and end up in the shipped HTML/JS — never put a secret in one.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN — Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon.
#
# ⚠️  LEAVE THIS UNSET. Setting it is a deliberate policy change, not config.
#
# Page views are collected at Cloudflare's EDGE instead (docs/12 D-56) — the
# dashboard reports them for any proxied site with no client script, no
# third-party request and no beacon. Do NOT set this variable in Cloudflare
# Pages -> Settings -> Environment variables either; that path was the whole
# reason this warning exists.
#
# Why it matters: the beacon was measured, and it POSTs ~933 bytes of RUM
# telemetry to cloudflareinsights.com a few seconds after load. It carries
# nothing about the user's files — but docs/06 §5 assertion (a) is absolute
# ("zero requests with a non-empty request body — ever"), and privacy.spec.ts
# calls failing it a release blocker with no exceptions. Setting this token
# WILL fail that suite, which is the intended safety net rather than an
# inconvenience to work around.
#
# The wiring is kept, tested and dormant so the decision stays reversible. To
# reverse it honestly, update docs/06 §5, /privacy and docs/12 D-56 in the same
# commit as the token — the guarantee moving from absolute to conditional is
# exactly what /privacy invites readers to check for.
PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOYMENT — read by scripts/deploy.mjs, never at build time, never shipped.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#   Scope it to Account -> Cloudflare Pages -> Edit and NOTHING else. A token
#   with broader scope can edit DNS and read billing; deploying needs neither,
#   and a deploy script is exactly the thing whose output ends up in a log.
#   Create at dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#   Cloudflare dashboard -> Workers & Pages -> the ID in the right-hand column.
#
# CF_PAGES_PROJECT   optional, defaults to "keptpix"
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
